Chapter: NarrowingUnproven

 The bounded-signatures campaign endgame: CDX2051 is an error. A
 value whose static range cannot be proven within a bounded
 position's declared bound no longer compiles - the flow is
 rejected, and the author either proves the range or asserts it with
 __narrow, which traps at runtime if violated. One definition per
 unproven shape the retired warnings covered: arithmetic over an
 unbounded operand, a plain body into a bounded return, a builtin
 fact wider than the target field, a plain parameter into a bounded
 field, a plain parameter into a bounded constructor payload, and a
 parameter reaching the store through a let-local.

Section: Definitions

  Slot = record {
   addr : Integer between 0 and 4294967295
  }

  table-base : Integer = 28968

  slot-at-wide : Integer -> Slot
  slot-at-wide (i) = Slot { addr = table-base + i * 8 }

  make-level : Integer -> Integer between 0 and 15
  make-level (n) = n

  Meta = record {
   tiny : Integer between 0 and 255
  }

  measure-tiny : List Integer -> Meta
  measure-tiny (xs) = Meta { tiny = list-length xs }

  Entry = record {
   code : Integer between 0 and 255
  }

  make-wide : Integer -> Entry
  make-wide (n) = Entry { code = n }

  Byteish =
   | MkByte (Integer between 0 and 255)

  make-byte-wide : Integer -> Byteish
  make-byte-wide (n) = MkByte n

  Meta2 = record {
   raw : Integer between 0 and 4294967295
  }

  measure-raw : Integer -> Meta2
  measure-raw (p) =
   let m = p
   in Meta2 { raw = m }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((slot-at-wide 9).addr))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (make-level 9))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((measure-tiny [1]).tiny))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((make-wide 9).code))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((measure-raw 7).raw))
  end
